course: dictionary
lesson: 13861
title: A word for a turning point
level: primary-6
stars: 2
explain: A juncture is a particular moment or point in time, especially an important one. When a story says «At this juncture, Mia had to choose», the words «at this juncture» mean «at this point».
explain: Juncture has a second meaning: a place where two things join, like a junction. «The road reached a juncture near the old bridge» means the roads meet there. The word is the same, but the sentence tells you which meaning is right.
explain: To check the meaning, swap in «point» or «junction». If «At this point, Mia had to choose» still makes sense, you have found the right meaning. Juncture is a formal word, so you will meet it in exams, stories and history writing.
fact: Juncture means a particular moment or point in time, especially an important one.
fact: «At this juncture» means «at this point».
fact: «At a critical juncture» means at an important point where something big may change.
fact: Juncture can also mean a place where two things join, like a junction.
fact: Juncture is a formal word, so it is common in exams and history writing.
exercise: «At this juncture, the children had to choose which path to take.» What does juncture mean here? | A bridge over a river | *A point in time when a choice must be made | A kind of loud noise | A type of bread
exercise: «The two pipes met at a juncture under the sink.» What does juncture mean here? | A moment in history | *A place where two things join | A loud noise | A small tool for cutting
exercise: Which phrase means the same as «at this juncture»? | at the back of the room | *at this point | at the bottom | in the cupboard
test: «At that juncture, the ship turned back towards the harbour.» What does juncture mean here? | A field of wheat | A kind of fish | *A particular important moment | A soft blanket
test: Which word is closest in meaning to juncture when it means a place where two things join? | feather | *junction | holiday | whisper
exam: «At a critical juncture in the story, the hero must decide whether to trust the stranger.» What does critical juncture most likely mean? | A rest stop with food | A map of the city | A dull part of the story with nothing happening | *An important point where something big may change
